	<key>readme</key>
	<string># Claude Rewrite

Rewrite selected text (or the clipboard) with Claude and paste it back.

* Hotkey: select text in any app, press the hotkey, pick a style. Alfred strips hotkeys on import, so set one (e.g. ⌃⌥R) on the Hotkey trigger.
* Keyword `rw`: works on the clipboard. Type a word to filter styles (`rw prof`), or type an instruction (`rw say yes to thursday`) to get a Custom item plus every style with that instruction added.

Backend:

* Claude subscription (default): uses your installed Claude Code and your Claude plan login. No API key needed. Run `claude` once in a terminal and sign in with your Claude account.
* Anthropic API key: paste the key in the API key field, or store it in the macOS Keychain instead:

      security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s anthropic-api-key -w
</string>
